---
Validate all JSON fields in project_load to prevent buffer overflows.

Malformed .sqproj files can contain out-of-range values that cause
array out-of-bounds access, integer overflow, or undefined behavior.

## Fields to validate
- num_tracks: clamp to 0..SQ_MAX_TRACKS (16)
- track.length: clamp to 1..SQ_MAX_STEPS (64)
- num_sections: clamp to 0..SQ_MAX_SECTIONS (32)
- unison_voices: clamp to 1..7
- synth_mode: validate enum range 0..2
- fm_algorithm: clamp to 0..7
- sample_index: clamp to 0..num_samples-1
- synth_preset: clamp to 0..num_synth_presets-1
- velocity: clamp to 0..127
- All float params: clamp to reasonable ranges (0..1 for most, 20..20000 for freq)

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Every JSON field read in project.c has bounds checking
- [ ] Invalid values are clamped (not rejected) so partial projects still load
- [ ] LOG_WARN for each clamped value
- [ ] No crash when loading a project with any out-of-range value

## Test Plan
- [ ] Malformed project test: create .sqproj with num_tracks=999, verify loads without crash
- [ ] Malformed project test: negative values, verify clamped to 0
- [ ] Malformed project test: missing fields, verify defaults applied
- [ ] ASan run: load malformed project, no buffer overflow
